Build palladium for wasm32-wasip1: bound recursion by the wasm stacks

Checking runs on worker threads with 256 MiB to 4 GiB stacks, sized for
MAX_DEPTH = 200 000 nested infer/whnf/def-eq calls. wasm32-wasip1 has no
threads, and its guest calls run on the engine's native stack (wasmfuzz:
8 MiB for run-input, 32 MiB per fuzzing worker): a whnf/reduce_nat chain
~60 000 levels deep (arena test perf/unfold-before-literal-bad) overflows
it. On wasm32 (and in --cfg fuzzing builds, so native replays agree)
MAX_DEPTH is 4096. The five depth guards in tc.rs also fault when less
than 2 MiB of the 16 MiB linear-memory stack (from __stack_low) is left;
util::stack_exhausted is false on native targets. Both end the declaration
with the existing "recursion depth exceeded" fault.
Upstream: none (no issues upstream; PRs #1-#3 are the author's own, checked 2026-11-22).

